# Communication and Clarification

## When to Ask Questions
- **ALWAYS** ask clarifying questions when requirements are ambiguous
- **NEVER** make assumptions about:
  - User authentication requirements
  - Data models and relationships
  - Business logic and validation rules
  - UI/UX preferences beyond basic implementation
  - Deployment environments
  - Third-party integrations
  
## What to Clarify
- Specific feature requirements and edge cases
- Database schema and relationships
- API endpoint specifications
- Authentication and authorization needs
- Performance requirements
- Browser/platform compatibility needs

---

**Remember**: When in doubt, ask for clarification rather than making assumptions. Better to confirm requirements upfront than to build the wrong thing.
